   "Step 1 parts were correct; no parts added or dropped.",
   "Piezo disc is modelled with the catalogue `buzzer` type. Pin 1 (black wire, lower voltage) goes to the GND column; pin 2 (red wire) goes to the A0 column, as the tutorial says.",
   "Breadboard coordinates are read from the image: piezo legs in columns 5 and 8, the 1 Mohm resistor bridging columns 5 and 8 (in parallel with the piezo), the black wire in column 5 and the red wire in column 8. The image's top half is labelled rows j-f; the catalogue calls this half bank 't' with rows a-e, so rows are mapped j->a, i->b, h->c, g->d, f->e. Which exact row is used does not change the connectivity.",
   "Black wire goes from Arduino GND (the GND pin next to pin 13, modelled as GND.1) to breadboard column 5; red wire goes from A0 to breadboard column 8.",
